{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_future_patterns", "label": "Future patterns", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Promises and actors are two concurrency models in one runtime; these helpers cross the bridge without blocking the mailbox.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_await_blocks_the_mailbox", "label": "await inside onReceive blocks the mailbox", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Only one onReceive invocation runs at a time and an await keeps that invocation alive until the promise settles, so the next message cannot be processed until then.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_pipeto", "label": "pipeTo", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Schedules a callback that tells the eventual result to a recipient, so the result lands as a normal message processed in order and the mailbox is never blocked.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_success_failure", "label": "Success and Failure envelopes", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Tagged immutable classes matched with instanceof; they stop a raw promise result being mistaken for a command when the receiving actor message type already includes arbitrary results.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_unwrapped_pipe", "label": "Unwrapped pipe drops rejections", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "With wrap false the raw fulfillment value is told and rejections are dropped silently, which suits a target expecting the value shape directly or errors handled elsewhere.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_after", "label": "after and CancellablePromise", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Waits via setTimeout then calls the factory once; the returned promise carries cancel, which clears the timer and rejects - useful for watchdog and race patterns.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_timers_comparison", "label": "after versus context.timers", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "context.timers delivers by tell to self and auto-cancels on actor stop; after resolves a promise and does not. Inside an actor prefer timers, outside or for a promise pipeline prefer after.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_futures_patterns_mdc_boundary", "label": "pipeTo does not carry MDC across the boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The promise resolves outside any LogContext.run scope, so the following tell may lose the correlation id; snapshot the context and re-enter it in a then if the result needs the same id.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/futures-patterns.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"sour